# The art under docs/art/ is generated. render_repo_art.py writes LF on every
# platform, so pin the checkout to LF as well and each file's byte count and
# SHA-256 stay the same whoever cloned the repository.
docs/art/*.svg text eol=lf
docs/art/*.json text eol=lf

# The smallharness fixture pack carries receipts whose fixtureFileHash is a
# SHA-256 over the fixture file's bytes. Without a pinned line ending those
# bytes differ by platform, so a receipt generated on Windows fails to verify on
# Linux and the reverse. That is not hypothetical: the committed hashes were
# CRLF, the pack verified on Windows, and it failed the moment CI ran it. Same
# reasoning as the generated art above.
demo/integrations/smallharness-dogfood-pack/** text eol=lf
